# The gun commands vis.mac applies, then a run - so that a macro-driven run can be compared
# against the same example in batch.
#
# This exists because the two disagreed by a third and nothing noticed. vis.mac set
# `/gun/beamRectangular 8 8 cm`; B1's generator draws its own spot and calls
# SetParticlePosition; the position was sampled twice and a third of the beam missed the
# detector. Batch said 429 pGy, interactive said 287, both looked reasonable, and the pipeline
# only ever ran batch. See docs/RISK.md V3 and tests/test_gun_position.cu.
#
# Every interactive path deserves a macro that a machine can run.
/control/verbose 0
/run/initialize
/gun/particle gamma
/gun/energy 6 MeV
# Deliberately set, and deliberately expected to make no difference: B1's generator sets the
# position per event, and a position means a point. If this line changes the answer, the
# extension has taken over a Geant4 method again.
/gun/beamRectangular 8 8 cm
/run/beamOn 10000
